  "question": {
    "text": "The temperature of two outer surfaces of a composite slab, consisting of two materials having coefficients of thermal conductivity $K$ and $2 K$ and thickness $x$ and $4 x$, respectively are $T_2$ and $T_1\\left(T_2>T_1\\right)$. The rate of heat transfer through the slab, in a steady state is $\\left(\\frac{A\\left(T_2-T_1\\right) K}{x}\\right) f$, with $f$ equal to\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/hqP8B6rNJuy4jVRR4908Y8vPLIJLljqlXSe9P5NSw8M.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NpxAD",
      "text": "\n1\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "A8uYS",
      "text": "\n$1 / 2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2Jalt",
      "text": "\n$2 / 3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "t1LKs",
      "text": "\n$1 / 3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\Delta \\mathrm{q}=\\frac{\\mathrm{kA}}{\\mathrm{x}}\\left[\\mathrm{T}_2-\\frac{2 \\mathrm{~T}_2-\\mathrm{T}_1}{3}\\right]$\n$=\\frac{\\mathrm{kA}}{3 \\mathrm{x}}\\left[\\mathrm{T}_2-\\mathrm{T}_1\\right]$",
    "image": null
  },
